nodecode-openmail is a rewrite of openmailsh's openmailsh/hermes-plugin:

  https://github.com/openmailsh/hermes-plugin
  commit 4035b7d1f8775304443f60f67bcd636acb1a325d

  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 OpenMail (LICENSE)

Rewritten in Common Lisp against Nodecode's cell contract: the nine tools
(openmail_whoami, openmail_send, openmail_reply, openmail_list_threads,
openmail_read_thread, openmail_list_messages, openmail_attachment_text,
openmail_list_inboxes, openmail_create_inbox) with their arguments, the
REST paths of the service they call, the in-thread reply that fills its
recipient and inbox in from the thread's last inbound message when the
caller names none, the read-state filter of the thread list, the default
inbox resolved from the section and then from the key's only one, the
server-side attachment text, and the anti-injection rule the original
ships as a skill, carried in the help topic.

Left out, because they are the Hermes gateway's surface rather than
Nodecode's, or because Nodecode's declarations have no way to say the
same thing: the websocket channel that wakes the agent on inbound mail
with its inbox/pod scoping and sender allow-list, attachment upload on
send and reply (the original confines model paths to its own media
folders), the `openmail` command-line tool for administration (sender
rules, pods, deleting an inbox, feedback), and the boolean `is_read`
thread filter, spelled `read_state` here because an absent boolean and a
false one are one value in a declared argument.
